1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,270
Blinkit took almost twenty-one thousand crore rupees in orders in just three months.

2
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:07,320
And for the first time, it's actually making money doing it.

3
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:10,478
So how does a ten-minute delivery app turn a profit?

4
00:00:10,478 --> 00:00:11,520
Let's break it down.

5
00:00:18,263 --> 00:00:24,773
Blinkit started in twenty thirteen as Grofers, an online grocery app founded by Albinder Dhindsa and Saurabh Kumar.

6
00:00:25,223 --> 00:00:27,206
For years it was a normal grocery app.

7
00:00:27,206 --> 00:00:30,024
Then in twenty twenty-one, it bet everything on speed:

8
00:00:30,024 --> 00:00:32,373
ten-minute delivery, and a new name, Blinkit.

9
00:00:32,823 --> 00:00:38,853
In twenty twenty-two, Zomato bought it for about four thousand four hundred crore rupees, paid in Zomato shares.

10
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:42,202
Today, Zomato's parent company is called Eternal.

11
00:00:42,202 --> 00:00:44,983
And Blinkit is now its biggest business by far.

12
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:47,361
Here's the first thing to understand:

13
00:00:47,361 --> 00:00:48,143
the dark store.

14
00:00:48,593 --> 00:00:51,764
A dark store is a small warehouse inside your neighbourhood.

15
00:00:51,764 --> 00:00:52,874
No customers walk in.

16
00:00:52,874 --> 00:00:56,573
It's packed with the few thousand things people order again and again.

17
00:00:57,023 --> 00:01:00,393
Because the store is close, the rider only goes a short distance.

18
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:03,763
The speed comes from where the store sits, not from fast driving.

19
00:01:04,213 --> 00:01:08,641
Blinkit had two thousand seven hundred and fifty-one dark stores at the end of September.

20
00:01:08,641 --> 00:01:12,423
It wants more than three thousand five hundred by March twenty twenty-seven.

21
00:01:12,873 --> 00:01:13,819
The second thing:

22
00:01:13,819 --> 00:01:15,543
Blinkit now owns what it sells.

23
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:21,726
In July twenty twenty-five, Eternal said Blinkit would start owning its stock, the way a supermarket does.

24
00:01:21,726 --> 00:01:24,863
So its revenue now counts the full price of what it sells.

25
00:01:25,313 --> 00:01:26,654
That's why revenue jumped.

26
00:01:26,654 --> 00:01:33,723
From July to September, Blinkit's revenue was nineteen thousand one hundred and fifty-two crore rupees, up ninety-four percent in a year.

27
00:01:34,173 --> 00:01:37,321
That's about seventy-nine percent of everything Eternal earns.

28
00:01:37,321 --> 00:01:40,673
The food delivery app that started it all is now the smaller part.

29
00:01:41,123 --> 00:01:42,435
But revenue isn't profit.

30
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:44,693
So where does the money actually come from?

31
00:01:45,143 --> 00:01:46,004
Two main places.

32
00:01:46,004 --> 00:01:47,995
The margin on every product it sells.

33
00:01:47,995 --> 00:01:51,923
And brands paying to show up first when you search, which is advertising.

34
00:01:52,373 --> 00:01:53,505
Here's the scorecard.

35
00:01:53,505 --> 00:01:58,085
A year ago, Blinkit lost one hundred and fifty-six crore rupees on an adjusted basis.

36
00:01:58,085 --> 00:02:01,103
This quarter, it made one hundred and eighty-four crore.

37
00:02:01,553 --> 00:02:05,490
That's less than one rupee of profit for every hundred rupees of orders.

38
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:08,333
Thin, but it has improved for six quarters in a row.

39
00:02:08,783 --> 00:02:12,360
And in its oldest cities, the margin is already above five percent.

40
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:13,588
That's the real signal:

41
00:02:13,588 --> 00:02:15,563
once a store matures, it makes money.

42
00:02:16,013 --> 00:02:19,413
Thirty-seven million people now order from Blinkit every month.

43
00:02:19,863 --> 00:02:20,870
So what's the catch?

44
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:22,733
Every new store loses money at first.

45
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:28,323
And Blinkit is opening hundreds of them, while Swiggy Instamart, Zepto and others fight for the same customers.

46
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:32,873
If the new stores mature like the old ones, Blinkit becomes a retail giant.

47
00:02:32,873 --> 00:02:35,223
If they don't, the profit disappears again.

48
00:02:35,673 --> 00:02:38,419
Should Blinkit grow faster, or make more money first?

49
00:02:38,419 --> 00:02:39,663
Tell me in the comments.

50
00:02:40,113 --> 00:02:40,678
Subscribe.

51
00:02:40,678 --> 00:02:41,412
On Wednesday:

52
00:02:41,412 --> 00:02:45,988
India's biggest Coca-Cola bottler wants to go public, and its revenue is falling.

53
00:02:45,988 --> 00:02:48,473
I'll explain why that isn't the whole story.
